  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total expiring contract value is $206B for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months. National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC holds the single largest expiring contract at $42.6B. Savannah River Nuclear Solutions LLC follows with $27.6B, and Lockheed Martin Services, LLC holds $20.6B. The Boeing Company, Chemonics International, Inc., Northrop Grumman Systems Corporation, and other large contractors also have major contract values expiring within this window. Expiring contract value is concentrated in four quarters: Jul-Sep 2026, Oct-Dec 2026, Jan-Mar 2027, and Apr-Jun 2027, which together account for most of the total; Jul-Sep 2027 contains a smaller residual. Award value figures represent total contract values for contracts with end dates in the next 12 months, not single-year obligations. End dates can be extended by options and modifications. This view highlights the set of high-value recompetes that federal contracting teams and industry partners will need to track during FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contracts represent the largest upcoming expirations?",
        "body": "National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC has the largest expiring contract at $42.6B. Savannah River Nuclear Solutions LLC has $27.6B and Lockheed Martin Services, LLC has $20.6B. Other notable expiring contracts include THE BOEING COMPANY at $7.6B and CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. at $6.7B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How are these expirations distributed across the next four quarters?",
        "body": "Jul-Sep 2026 contains $59.8B of expiring contract value. Oct-Dec 2026 contains $41.3B, Jan-Mar 2027 contains $40.3B, and Apr-Jun 2027 contains $62.2B. Jul-Sep 2027 contains $2.6B as a smaller remainder."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which large federal contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Large federal contracts expiring soon include National Technology & Engineering Solutions of Sandia, LLC at $42.6B, Savannah River Nuclear Solutions LLC at $27.6B, and Lockheed Martin Services, LLC at $20.6B. The list of top expirations also includes THE BOEING COMPANY at $7.6B, CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. at $6.7B, NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION at $5.4B, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $5B and $4.6B listings, BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION at $5B, and HUNTINGTON INGALLS INC at $3.7B. Total expiring contract value in the next 12 months is $206B."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a contract recompete?",
      "a": "A contract recompete is the process of competitively awarding a follow-on contract when an existing contract's period of performance ends. A recompete can involve the incumbent, other contractors, or a mix of sources of supply depending on the solicitation and procurement strategy. Contract end dates, options, and modifications can affect whether and when a recompete occurs."
    },
    {
      "q": "How current is this recompete data?",
      "a": "This recompete data covers FY2026 to date. Award value figures are total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months, and end dates can be extended by options and modifications."
    }
  ],
